---
// src/pages/kurzy/strategicka-praca-s-polarizaciou.astro
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout title="How to Work Strategically with Polarisation | Dialogue Centre">
  <!-- THREE DATES PREVIEW -->
  <section
    class="w-full px-8 py-12 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-emerald-50 dark:from-gray-800 dark:to-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"
  >
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto text-center">
      <h1
        class="mt-2 text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-[#102756] dark:text-white"
      >
        How to Work Strategically with Polarisation?
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
        Choose the date and location that works best for you.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="#registration"
          class="flex-1 min-w-[160px] px-6 py-4 rounded-lg bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 text-white font-semibold shadow-md hover:shadow-lg hover:opacity-90 transition-all duration-200 transform hover:scale-105"
        >
          <p class="text-xs opacity-90">24 September</p>
          <p class="text-lg">Banská Bystrica</p>
        </a>
        <a
          href="#registration"
          class="flex-1 min-w-[160px] px-6 py-4 rounded-lg bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 text-white font-semibold shadow-md hover:shadow-lg hover:opacity-90 transition-all duration-200 transform hover:scale-105"
        >
          <p class="text-xs opacity-90">1 October</p>
          <p class="text-lg">Trnava</p>
        </a>
        <a
          href="#registration"
          class="flex-1 min-w-[160px] px-6 py-4 rounded-lg bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 text-white font-semibold shadow-md hover:shadow-lg hover:opacity-90 transition-all duration-200 transform hover:scale-105"
        >
          <p class="text-xs opacity-90">9 October</p>
          <p class="text-lg">Online</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="relative w-full bg-[#102756] overflow-hidden">
    <div
      class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10"
      style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle, #fff 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 32px 32px;"
    >
    </div>
    <div class="relative max-w-5xl mx-auto px-8 py-24">
      <span class="text-sm font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-blue-300"
        >Training course</span
      >
      <h1
        class="mt-4 text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold text-white leading-tight max-w-3xl"
      >
        How to Work Strategically with Polarisation?
      </h1>
      <ul class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 max-w-2xl">
        <li
          class="flex items-start gap-3 text-blue-100 text-lg leading-relaxed"
        >
          <span class="mt-2 w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Do you want to quickly assess polarised situations and choose an effective
          depolarisation strategy?
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-start gap-3 text-blue-100 text-lg leading-relaxed"
        >
          <span class="mt-2 w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Do you want to better understand how attitudes, language, and communication
          contribute to polarisation — or help reduce it?
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-start gap-3 text-blue-100 text-lg leading-relaxed"
        >
          <span class="mt-2 w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Are you looking for ways to respond to “us versus them” dynamics before
          they become toxic or escalate into conflict?
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-start gap-3 text-blue-100 text-lg leading-relaxed"
        >
          <span class="mt-2 w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Do you want to create real depolarisation impact in your work, community,
          or organisation?
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 text-white/70 text-lg italic max-w-xl">
        If you answered yes to any of these questions, this course is designed
        for you.
      </p>
      <a
        href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdxDD6j4m8bGqPMq7U73ZdoppLMCwKXHU8a26iX1n7NrrHQDg/viewform"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 text-white font-semibold px-4 py-2.5 rounded-lg hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity text-sm"
      >
        Register
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHY POLARISATION -->
  <section class="w-full px-8 py-20 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <h2
        class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white"
      >
        Why focus on polarisation?
        <div
          class="h-1 w-20 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 mt-2 rounded-full"
        >
        </div>
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
        <div
          class="lg:col-span-2 flex flex-col gap-5 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-lg leading-relaxed"
        >
          <p>
            Polarisation — the <strong class="text-[#102756] dark:text-white"
              >“us versus them”</strong
            >
            mindset — is a natural part of interactions between groups of people and
            is not inherently negative. It is a common social phenomenon that appears
            in democratic debate, civic engagement, and efforts to bring about change.
          </p>
          <p>
            It can be seen in politics, urban planning, public administration,
            and interpersonal relationships — among world leaders, family
            members, colleagues, and communities, both locally and globally.
          </p>
          <p>
            It becomes a risk when it escalates into
            <strong class="text-[#102756] dark:text-white"
              >toxic polarisation</strong
            >. At that point, it undermines trust, weakens dialogue and
            cooperation, deepens conflict, and negatively affects democracy,
            public institutions, and social cohesion.
          </p>
          <p class="font-medium text-[#102756] dark:text-blue-300">
            This course will help you recognise this dynamic and work with it
            strategically.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="p-6 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 shadow-md self-start"
        >
          <p
            class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4"
          >
            Where polarisation appears
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span
              class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-sm bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-900/40 dark:text-blue-300"
              >Politics</span
            >
            <span
              class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-sm bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-900/40 dark:text-blue-300"
              >Urban planning</span
            >
            <span
              class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-sm bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-900/40 dark:text-blue-300"
              >Public administration</span
            >
            <span
              class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-sm bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-900/40 dark:text-blue-300"
              >Interpersonal relationships</span
            >
            <span
              class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-sm bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-900/40 dark:text-blue-300"
              >Religion & culture</span
            >
            <span
              class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-sm bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-900/40 dark:text-blue-300"
              >Rural vs. urban</span
            >
            <span
              class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-sm bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-900/40 dark:text-blue-300"
              >Organisations</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT WE OFFER -->
  <section class="w-full px-8 py-20 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <h2
        class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white"
      >
        What we offer and what you will gain
        <div
          class="h-1 w-20 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 mt-2 rounded-full"
        >
        </div>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-2xl">
        The course was developed in collaboration with Bart Brandsma, an
        internationally recognised Dutch expert in strategic approaches to
        polarisation. The goal of the course is not to eliminate polarisation,
        but to help participants work consciously and strategically with
        polarised situations in the public sphere.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
        <div
          class="p-6 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl shadow-md bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 flex flex-col gap-3 hover:border-blue-400/50 transition-colors duration-200"
        >
          <span class="text-3xl">🧭</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white">
            Brandsma’s depolarisation framework
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            A clear and practical framework for understanding the “us vs. them”
            dynamic.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="p-6 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl shadow-md bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 flex flex-col gap-3 hover:border-blue-400/50 transition-colors duration-200"
        >
          <span class="text-3xl">🗺️</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white">
            Polarisation map
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            An analytical tool for quickly diagnosing specific polarised
            situations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="p-6 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl shadow-md bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 flex flex-col gap-3 hover:border-blue-400/50 transition-colors duration-200"
        >
          <span class="text-3xl">🎯</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white">
            Four key depolarisation interventions
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Concrete interventions with direct impact on polarised situations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="p-6 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl shadow-md bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 flex flex-col gap-3 hover:border-blue-400/50 transition-colors duration-200"
        >
          <span class="text-3xl">📋</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white">
            Seven-step depolarisation strategy
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            A structured approach to planning and implementing a concrete
            depolarisation strategy.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="p-6 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl shadow-md bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 flex flex-col gap-3 hover:border-blue-400/50 transition-colors duration-200"
        >
          <span class="text-3xl">🧑💼</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white">
            Depolarisation leadership
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Principles of middle-ground leadership and reflection on your own
            style in polarised situations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="p-6 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl shadow-md bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 flex flex-col gap-3 hover:border-blue-400/50 transition-colors duration-200"
        >
          <span class="text-3xl">🧰</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white">
            Practical toolbox
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Tools tested on case studies and situations from your own
            professional environment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        class="mt-6 p-5 rounded-xl border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-900 bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-950/40 flex items-start gap-4"
      >
        <span class="text-xl mt-0.5">👥</span>
        <p class="text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-200 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The course takes place in a small group (<strong
            >min. 8 – max. 16 participants</strong
          >). We use <em>Art of Hosting</em> facilitation methods to create a pleasant,
          trusting, and safe atmosphere.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHO IS IT FOR -->
  <section class="w-full px-8 py-20 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <h2
        class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white"
      >
        Who is the course for?
        <div
          class="h-1 w-20 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 mt-2 rounded-full"
        >
        </div>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-2xl">
        The course is intended for everyone who encounters polarised situations
        and cares about democracy, social cohesion, and effective public policy.
        It is aimed especially at so-called “neutral” professionals:
      </p>

      <ul class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
        <li
          class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm"
        >
          <span
            class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Experts and facilitators of participatory processes and cross-sector collaboration
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm"
        >
          <span
            class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Mediators and conflict resolution professionals
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm"
        >
          <span
            class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Communication experts and strategists
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm"
        >
          <span
            class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Mayors, town leaders, and public officials
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm"
        >
          <span
            class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Political party leaders and members
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm"
        >
          <span
            class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Diplomatic staff
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm"
        >
          <span
            class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Civil servants and public policy makers
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm"
        >
          <span
            class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Law enforcement officers
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm"
        >
          <span
            class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Educators and academic staff
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm"
        >
          <span
            class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 shrink-0"
          ></span>
          Community leaders
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LECTURERS -->
  <section class="w-full px-8 py-20 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <h2
        class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white"
      >
        Course Lecturers
        <div
          class="h-1 w-20 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 mt-2 rounded-full"
        >
        </div>
      </h2>

      <div
        class="mt-10 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 shadow-md bg-white dark:bg-gray-900"
      >
        <div class="w-full aspect-[22/9]">
          <img
            src="https://storage.googleapis.com/dialogue-center/team-members/soniacka_miska1.png"
            alt="Michaela Kováčik Huľuková and Soňa Kariková"
            class="w-full h-full object-cover object-[center_60%]"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 md:p-8">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white">
                Michaela Kováčik Huľuková
              </h2>
              <p
                class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"
              >
                She comes from Banská Bystrica and earned her Master of Laws
                degree at Comenius University in Bratislava. After completing
                her studies, she completed a nine-month internship at the Czech
                Women’s Lobby in Prague, where she worked as an assistant
                project manager. Since 2022, she has served as the director of
                Dialogue Centre.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white">
                Soňa Kariková
              </h2>
              <p
                class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"
              >
                Soňa leads the Department of Participation and Innovation in
                Open Governance at the City Office in Banská Bystrica. She is
                also involved in the OGP Local initiative, where she supports
                transparency and partnership. As the founder of DC and an expert
                in democratic innovation, she also brings experience from
                business psychology, which she studied in London.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LOGISTICS & REGISTRATION -->
  <section
    id="registration"
    class="w-full px-8 py-20 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900"
  >
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <h2
        class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white"
      >
        Dates and registration
        <div
          class="h-1 w-20 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 mt-2 rounded-full"
        >
        </div>
      </h2>

      <div
        class="mt-6 p-5 rounded-xl border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-900 bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-950/40 flex items-start gap-3"
      >
        <span class="text-lg mt-0.5">⏰</span>
        <p class="text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-200 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <strong>Early bird discount:</strong> Save €30 by registering before the
          stated deadline.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <!-- BANSKÁ BYSTRICA -->
        <div
          class="p-6 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl shadow-md bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 flex flex-col gap-4"
        >
          <div>
            <span
              class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-900/40 dark:text-blue-300"
              >In-person</span
            >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white mt-3"
            >
              Banská Bystrica
            </h3>
          </div>
          <dl class="text-sm space-y-3">
            <div>
              <dt
                class="text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-xs uppercase font-semibold"
              >
                Date
              </dt>
              <dd class="font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white">
                24 September 2026
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt
                class="text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-xs uppercase font-semibold"
              >
                Venue
              </dt>
              <dd class="font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white">
                365 Lab
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt
                class="text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-xs uppercase font-semibold"
              >
                Time
              </dt>
              <dd class="font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white">
                9:00 – 16:00
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt
                class="text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-xs uppercase font-semibold"
              >
                Price
              </dt>
              <dd class="font-semibold text-[#102756] dark:text-white text-lg">
                €160
              </dd>
              <div
                class="mt-2 p-2 rounded bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-900/20 border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800"
              >
                <p class="text-xs text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300">
                  <strong>Early Bird:</strong> €130 until 24 Aug
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <a
            href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdxDD6j4m8bGqPMq7U73ZdoppLMCwKXHU8a26iX1n7NrrHQDg/viewform"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-emerald-500 text-white font-semibold px-4 py-2.5 rounded-lg hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity text-sm"
          >
            Register
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- TRNAVA -->
        <div
          class="p-6 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl shadow-md bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 flex flex-col gap-4"
        >
